# customer-template-rating and customer-template-rates

Full guidance: `.cursor/skills/rlm-customer-demo-usage-rates/SKILL.md` and its
`reference.md`.

## Load order

PCM first (SKUs + UOM), then rating, then rates. Activations run after SFDMU:
`activate_rating_records`, then `activate_rates`.

Deleting: `delete_customer_demo_rates_data` **before** `delete_customer_demo_rating_data` —
`RateCardEntry` references the meters, so UsageResource delete fails otherwise.

## Silent failures to design around

- **`ProductUsageGrant`** — SFDMU v5 reports "1 processed, 0 failed" while nothing persists.
  Always verify with SOQL after load; fall back to Apex insert plus activation.
- **`UsageGrantRenewalPolicy`, `UsageGrantRolloverPolicy`, `UsageOveragePolicy`** — SFDMU
  silently fails to create these. Reference policies that **already exist** in the org
  (e.g. `SF-DEMO-USG-RENEW`, `SF-DEMO-USG-ROLL`, `Default Usage Overage Policy`). Query for
  exact names; `Default Overage` is not the same as `Default Usage Overage Policy`.

## Parent resolution (SFDMU v5)

`UsageResource.csv` needs `UnitOfMeasureClass.Name` and `DefaultUnitOfMeasure.Name` — the
`.Code` / `.UnitCode` columns alone do not resolve. `ProductUsageGrant.csv` needs
`UnitOfMeasure.Name` and `UnitOfMeasureClass.Name`. Check
`reports/MissingParentRecordsReport.csv` when counts look wrong.

## UsageModelType

Sellable usage SKUs use **`Anchor`**, not `Pack`. `Pack` makes the platform reject
`ProductUsageResourcePolicy` and can fail quote save with
`PlaceSalesTransactionPersistException`.

## Rate cards

`RateCardEntry.ProductSellingModel` must match the SKU's Standard `PricebookEntry` in
`scripts/customer-demo/customer-pricebook-entries.csv` — on **both** Base and Tier rows.

Base rows carry `Rate`. Tier rows leave `Rate` empty; stepped bands go on
**`RateAdjustmentByTier`** (not `PriceAdjustmentTier`, which belongs to
`PriceAdjustmentSchedule`). Keep `RateCardEntry` before `RateAdjustmentByTier` in
`export.json` so RABT inserts while the parent is still `Draft`.

Quote the sellable `*-USG-*` SKUs, never the `*-BLNG-*` usage-definition products.
